      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added `emptyCharArrayTokenRejected` new char[0] already throws via the length \u003d\u003d 0 check, so no production code needed to change.\n\nOn printable-ASCII: we don\u0027t interpret the token\u0027s contents, and different providers use different token formats, so I only reject CR/LF (the header-injection risk) and leave the rest to the server. I can tighten it to reject anything outside printable ASCII if you\u0027d prefer.",
