      "writtenOn": "2026-09-26T20:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t the Java compiler smart enough to use a StringBuilder under the hood if we simply do\n```\nconn.setRequestHeader(HDR_AUTHORIZATION, type.getSchemeName() + \u0027 \u0027 + token);\n```\n?",
      "revId": "3a3abd1c9028f7442f00751fd1250c961728a969",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eeb5d3c2_d4a15fa3",
        "filename": "org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/transport/HttpAuthMethod.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 353,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000177
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-27T14:54:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The compiler would indeed use a StringBuilder for +, so that\u0027s not the concern. The catch is that token is a char[]: with + token the + takes the Object path and appends the array\u0027s identity (Bearer [C@…), not the characters.\n\nAppending it as a char[] (StringBuilder.append(char[]), or String.valueOf(token)) is what yields the actual token — which is why the explicit builder is kept. (Also, the method is setRequestProperty.)",
      "parentUuid": "c78ad567_db26b6b1",
      "revId": "3a3abd1c9028f7442f00751fd1250c961728a969",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    }
